{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>They break out.</b> A term of breaking out — and likewise הִטּוֹחַ. But ״חִלֵּץ אֶת הָאֲבָנִים״ — the term is turned to refer to the person who removed them, and its pattern is like כָּבֵד, כִּפֵּר, דִּבֵּר." "<b>And if the plague returns, etc.</b> I might think if it returned on the same day it is impure — therefore Scripture says ״וְשָׁב הַכֹּהֵן״ ״וְאִם יָשׁוּב״: just as the שִׁיבָה mentioned below is at the end of a week, so too the שִׁיבָה mentioned here is at the end of a week (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:31.455589209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}